From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adi Hanif <adihanifsdr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 15:41:58 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] i386/kvm: QEMU_IDENTITY_KVM_SIGNATURE for the CPUID
 0x40000000 signature

The KVM paravirt leaf advertises "KVMKVMKVM" (NUL padded to 12 bytes)
whenever the CPU exposes KVM. Take the signature from the environment
when set, truncated / NUL padded to 12 bytes. Note that a guest kernel
only binds kvm-clock and the other KVM paravirt features when it finds
the canonical signature, so a different one also hides those - which is
the point when it is used.
---
 target/i386/kvm/kvm.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/i386/kvm/kvm.c b/target/i386/kvm/kvm.c
index a0bc9ea7..49954989 100644
--- a/target/i386/kvm/kvm.c
+++ b/target/i386/kvm/kvm.c
@@ -42,6 +42,7 @@
 #include "qemu/ratelimit.h"
 #include "qemu/config-file.h"
 #include "qemu/error-report.h"
+#include "qemu/identity.h"
 #include "qemu/memalign.h"
 #include "hw/i386/x86.h"
 #include "hw/i386/kvm/xen_evtchn.h"
@@ -1855,7 +1856,9 @@ int kvm_arch_init_vcpu(CPUState *cs)
         abort();
 #endif
     } else if (cpu->expose_kvm) {
-        memcpy(signature, "KVMKVMKVM\0\0\0", 12);
+        /* "KVMKVMKVM" unless QEMU_IDENTITY_KVM_SIGNATURE says otherwise */
+        qemu_identity_fixed("KVM_SIGNATURE", "KVMKVMKVM",
+                            (char *)signature, 12, '\0');
         c = &cpuid_data.entries[cpuid_i++];
         c->function = KVM_CPUID_SIGNATURE | kvm_base;
         c->eax = KVM_CPUID_FEATURES | kvm_base;
